.TH IVS-SESSIONS-BROWSER 1 "2026-06-01" "ivs-sessions-browser" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ivs-sessions-browser \- browse IVS session schedules in a terminal UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ivs-sessions-browser
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ivs-sessions-browser
is a curses-based terminal browser for IVS master and intensive session
schedules. It fetches session tables, displays them in a keyboard-driven TUI,
supports filtering and sorting, and can export formatted text, colored PDF, or
XLSX spreadsheet output.
.PP
User-editable configuration files are stored in
.IR ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/ .
Use
.B --init-config
to create default configuration files without starting the TUI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --year " YEAR"
Year expression to fetch. Accepted forms include
.BR 2026 ,
.BR 2024,2025 ,
and
.BR 2022-2026 .
Defaults to the current year.
When omitted, a configured value in
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/startup_defaults.json
is used first.
.TP
.BI --scope " master|intensive|both"
Select which schedules to include. Defaults to
.BR both .
When omitted, a configured value in
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/startup_defaults.json
is used first.
.TP
.BI --filters " EXPR"
Apply an initial filter expression.
When omitted, a configured value in
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/startup_defaults.json
is used first.
.TP
.BI -o ", " --output " FILE"
Write formatted output to
.IR FILE
and exit. Use
.B -
for standard output.
.TP
.BI -p ", " --pretty-print " COLUMNS"
Select output columns. Use
.B ALL
or pipe-delimited column names such as
.BR OP|START|CODE|STATIONS|CORR .
.TP
.BI --format " text|pdf|xlsx"
Select output format. Defaults to
.BR text .
PDF preserves row colors in a monospaced layout; XLSX writes spreadsheet cells
with headers, filters, frozen first row, clickable code links, and operator row
colors. Code links keep the same font color as the rest of the row.
.TP
.B -a, --append
Append text output to the output file instead of overwriting it.
PDF and XLSX exports always write a new file.
.TP
.B -m, --mirrors
Check configured mirror sites and use the most recently updated source.
When omitted, a configured value in
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/startup_defaults.json
is used first.
.TP
.B --no-mirrors
Disable mirror checking even if startup defaults enable it.
.TP
.B --verbose-fetch
Show fetch progress even when writing output to a file or stdout.
.TP
.B --import-local
Import local
.B .vex
and
.B .skd
session files from the current directory into
.IR ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/manual_sessions.json .
Already-known session codes are skipped.
Imported sessions are merged into the current view before filtering, sorting,
and export.
.TP
.B --init-config
Create default user configuration files in
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/
and exit.
.TP
.B --man
Show this manual page and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Show package version and exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help and exit.
.SH FILTERS
Filter expressions use
.B field:value
clauses. Multiple clauses separated by
.B ;
are combined with AND.
.PP
Examples:
.TP
.B code:R1|R4
Show sessions whose code contains R1 or R4.
.TP
.B stations:Nn&Ns
Show sessions with both Nn and Ns active.
.TP
.B stations_removed:Ft|Ur
Show sessions where Ft or Ur appears in the removed station set.
.TP
.B start:jun
Show sessions starting in June, regardless of year. Month names and 3-letter
abbreviations are accepted for the start field.
.TP
.B op:Alice|Bob
Show sessions assigned to Alice or Bob.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Up/Down, PgUp/PgDn, Home/End
Move around the session list.
.TP
.B T
Jump to today's session.
.TP
.B /
Enter or edit a filter expression.
.TP
.B F1-F12
Toggle a start-month filter from January through December. Other filter clauses
are preserved.
.TP
.B C
Clear filters.
.TP
.B D
Save the current filter as the startup default. If no filter is active, clear
the saved default filter.
.TP
.B A, +
Add a manual session inline. Use Tab and Shift+Tab to move between fields,
Enter to save, and Esc to cancel.
Fields are Type, Code, Start, Dur, Stations, Ops, and Corr.
.TP
.B Del
Delete the selected manual session from
.IR manual_sessions.json .
Fetched IVS sessions are not removed.
.TP
.B 0
Clear the selected session's operator assignment.
.TP
.B 1-5
Assign the configured operator for that key to the selected session.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected session page in the default browser.
.TP
.B ?
Show inline help.
.TP
.B P
Export visible rows to a timestamped PDF and open it.
.TP
.B X
Export visible rows to a timestamped XLSX workbook and open it.
.TP
.B S
Show the session statistics dialog.
.TP
.B G
Save and open a station contribution plot. Repeated presses cycle session
share, hours, and weighted hours.
.TP
.B q, Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/operators.json
Operator key bindings and row colors. Created from packaged defaults when
missing. Keys 1-5 default to U1-U5 and should be edited for local use.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/operator_assignments.json
Persistent mapping of session code to assigned operator label.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/manual_sessions.json
User-maintained sessions merged into the normal row list before filtering,
sorting, and export. Created with an empty
.B sessions
list and an example object when missing.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/pdf_columns
Default PDF export columns. Created as
.B op|start|code|stations|corr
when missing.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/startup_defaults.json
Optional startup defaults for omitted
.BR --year ,
.BR --scope ,
.BR --filters ,
and
.BR --mirrors .
.TP
.I ~/.config/ivs-sessions-browser/app_state.json
Internal UI state, including the last version whose "what's new" notes were
shown.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ivs-sessions-browser --init-config
Create editable config files and exit.
.TP
.B ivs-sessions-browser --year 2026 --scope both
Browse master and intensive sessions for 2026.
.TP
.B ivs-sessions-browser --year 2026 --filters 'code:R1|R4; stations:Nn'
Start the TUI with an initial filter.
.TP
.B ivs-sessions-browser --year 2026 --import-local
Import local VEX/SKD session files, then show the selected year in the TUI.
.TP
.B ivs-sessions-browser --year 2026 --output sessions.pdf --format pdf -p OP|START|CODE|STATIONS|CORR
Export selected columns to a PDF.
.TP
.B ivs-sessions-browser --year 2026 --output sessions.xlsx --format xlsx -p OP|START|CODE|STATIONS|CORR
Export selected columns to an XLSX workbook.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
Full documentation is available at:
.br
.I https://github.com/jonleithe/ivs_sessions_browser/tree/v4/docs
